# Brand and prose

## Names

- Product: Good Standing
- Trading: Good Standing Software (no Ltd)
- Legal: Good Standing Software Ltd (17423889)
- Never write that the company “trades as Good Standing”

## Document titles

Home: `Good Standing | …` (brand first). Other pages: `{Topic} | Good Standing` (brand last). Separator is `|` only. Use the product name, not trading or legal. Keep `<title>`, `og:title`, and `twitter:title` the same. If JSON-LD `WebPage` `name` or `headline` duplicates the title, keep it in sync.

Locked titles:

- Home: `Good Standing | software for UK membership bodies`
- Privacy: `Privacy notice | Good Standing`
- Thanks: `Thanks | Good Standing`

## Voice

- Holding pages and `/thanks/`: company **we**, not “I’m Mark…”
- Approachable, professional, intriguing. Not matey. Not salesy.
- Research before product; nothing to buy. No product-launch CTA grid.
- Do not use “CPD” in marketing, survey, or outreach — say continuing education, fees, membership, or good standing
- Outreach is first-person Mark (Director) and lives in Gmail. See Outreach.

## Tone

- Home / thanks: letterhead — short, research posture
- Privacy: ICO-style notice. Do not gut legal structure or rewrite it for spacing or tone
- Outreach email: first-person Mark; same letter to everyone; research, not a pitch

## Outreach

Same subject and body for every recipient. Do not write as if we know the organisation — no org name in the subject, no AMS, hours, register, size, or other on-file facts.

Only these change per send:

- `To`
- Survey URL `ref` and `email` (`email` URL-encoded)

Do not add `organisation=`, per-org `utm_content`, or any other query param. Site, Companies House, ICO, and privacy links stay identical.

Locked subject: `A Short Survey`

Locked letter (HTML in Gmail; linked words in **bold**):

```
Hello,

I'm Mark from Good Standing Software. We're researching how UK professional bodies handle membership, fees and good standing.

Before building anything, we want to know whether there's a real need — and where the manual work becomes messy enough that software would actually help.

The **survey** is confidential, there's nothing to buy, and it takes about 5–7 minutes. Your help would be greatly appreciated.

Thanks,

Mark

**Good Standing Software Ltd**
Registered in England and Wales.
Company no. **17423889**. ICO no. **ZC233855**.
71-75 Shelton Street, Covent Garden, London WC2H 9JQ

**Privacy notice**

To opt out, please reply **stop**.
```

Links (clean `href`, `target="_blank"`):

- **survey** → `https://research.goodstanding.co.uk/r/Bz5oLN?ref={ref}&email={urlencoded-email}`
- **Good Standing Software Ltd** → `https://goodstanding.co.uk/?utm_source=survey&utm_medium=email&utm_campaign=research`
- **17423889** → `https://find-and-update.company-information.service.gov.uk/company/17423889`
- **ZC233855** → `https://ico.org.uk/ESDWebPages/Entry/ZC233855`
- **Privacy notice** → `https://goodstanding.co.uk/privacy/?utm_source=survey&utm_medium=email&utm_campaign=research`

- Open with `Hello,` on its own line. Close is `Thanks,` then `Mark` — not `Thanks in advance,`
- **survey** is the only bold in the body; **stop** is the only bold in the footer
- Say `Privacy notice`, not `Privacy policy`
- UTM order is `utm_source`, `utm_medium`, `utm_campaign`
- The Gmail API rewrites `href`s to `google.com/url`. Write clean URLs; finish the links in the Gmail UI so the stored MIME stays clean
- Drafts live in Gmail (`mark@goodstanding.co.uk`). Do not invent email files
- Do not mark CRM Survey status Link sent or set Last surveyed until Mark actually sends. See `crm.mdc`

## Links

Internal directory links keep a trailing slash (`privacy/`, `../`, `./`).

## Checklist (public HTML)

- Titles / `og:title` / `twitter:title` (and matching JSON-LD name) in sync
- Brand position: home brand-first; inner pages topic-first
- Separator `|` in titles only; body may keep em dashes
- We-voice on holding pages
- Names lock
- Meta descriptions match the page (privacy is a notice, not a pitch)
- H1 aligns with the title topic (`Thanks` on `/thanks/`)
- Footer Survey `?ref=footer`; homepage survey `?ref=homepage`
- External links: `target="_blank"` `rel="noopener noreferrer"`

